Rationale: this compiler must not share the plain0.1.15 persistent cache
identity with older source snapshots. The full immutable pre-metadata tree
is encoded through the existing VERSION/package/cache-key mechanism; no
circular final-tree hash or discovery of an unrelated native library.
Re-keyed from the b1367a59 refresh (e808dbdd…) for the ac88f5bc pin, whose
two new upstream commits (FFI Layout serialization, docs) move the
pre-metadata tree.

Quality: VERSION is the sole source delta in this patch. Algorithms, kernel
outputs and numerical contracts are unchanged. Preserve old namespaces.
Before first gate and first serving use on every rank, verify the new actual
host namespace is absent, then actual module/distribution/pin/base-key
version and namespace agree. Import and loaded-library hashes remain required.

Tests: reviewed NO_VERSION_LABEL=1 provider/PEP440/CMake/backend mechanism;
new literal provider/wheel/cache-key checks remain source-only. Full Linux
wheel/image and every first native gate remain mandatory. No performance
claim or repeated qualification of C42/C44 is implied.

Upstream status: local source/provenance correction; not submitted.
